---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DEMO_CODESPACE_URL, DEMO_DEVCONTAINER } from '../lib/runNow';

const title = 'Install Sounio';
const description =
  'Open the demo Codespace, or clone and run examples/hello.sio. Linux x86-64 has a committed prebuilt. macOS ARM64 builds from source. Windows has no path.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="section-shell">
    <div class="container install">
      <span class="badge-pill">Install</span>
      <h1>Install Sounio</h1>
      <p lang="en">Status: Sounio 3.0 (pre-release).</p>
      <p>
        Two ways to a first program. Neither one is a one-line installer, and neither one runs on Windows.
        The repository does not publish a stdlib tarball separate from the git tree.
      </p>

      <h2>GitHub Codespaces</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={DEMO_CODESPACE_URL}>Open in GitHub Codespaces</a>
        uses <code>{DEMO_DEVCONTAINER}</code> (Ubuntu 24.04, 4 CPUs, 16 GB).
        After the container is created, <code>scripts/demo_env_setup.sh</code> installs a C toolchain if it is missing, installs elan, and materialises the committed Madaros prebuilt.
        The editor opens <code>TOUR.md</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This page did not create a Codespace, so it does not report how long creation takes.
        The setup script's own comment says <code>bash scripts/tour.sh</code> is about 35 seconds once that setup has finished.
        The host requirement of 16 GB spends a free quota faster than a small container.
      </p>
      <p>In the repository root:</p>
      <pre><code>export SOUNIO_STDLIB_PATH="$PWD/stdlib"
./bin/souc check examples/hello.sio
./bin/souc run examples/hello.sio</code></pre>
      <p>
        The program prints <code>Hello, Sounio</code>. The compiler prints a log before that line.
        Exit status 0. Measured on Linux x86-64 on 20 November 2026 with the committed prebuilt
        (<code>bin/madaros-linux-x86_64.gz</code>, commit <code>4b7b96ea2</code>).
        <code>./bin/souc --version</code> prints an identity line. This page does not quote it.
      </p>

      <h2>Linux x86-64, without Codespaces</h2>
      <p>
        Needs <code>git</code>, <code>bash</code>, <code>gzip</code>, <code>sha256sum</code>, and about 2 GB free.
        <code>INSTALL.md</code> records a shallow clone of 1.1 GB on 27 October 2026 at <code>75fd75c58</code>.
        That size was not re-measured for this page.
      </p>
      <pre><code>git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/Sounio-lang/sounio.git
cd sounio
export SOUNIO_STDLIB_PATH="$PWD/stdlib"
./bin/souc check examples/hello.sio
./bin/souc run examples/hello.sio</code></pre>
      <p>
        The first <code>./bin/souc</code> decompresses <code>bin/madaros-linux-x86_64.gz</code>.
        After that file exists, the checksum is <code>(cd bin &amp;&amp; sha256sum -c madaros-linux-x86_64.sha256)</code>.
        A match prints <code>madaros-linux-x86_64: OK</code>.
        Do not start from <code>cargo build</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>macOS ARM64</h2>
      <p>
        The Linux ELF does not run. Build the native artifact first, following
        <a href="https://github.com/Sounio-lang/sounio/blob/main/docs/compiler/MADAROS_MACOS_ARM64.md">the macOS ARM64 guide</a>.
        That build needs a signed current-source bootstrap seed, C++23 <code>clang++</code>, <code>codesign</code>, <code>timeout</code>, and Boost headers.
        The full install gate also needs a real Metal device.
      </p>

      <h2>Windows</h2>
      <p>This repository has no Windows install path.</p>

      <p>
        The program and the next pages are in <a href="/learn/getting-started/">Getting started</a>.
        The browser page is a syntax preview with simulated output: <a href="/playground/">Playground</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .install { max-width: 760px; display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.1; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  p { color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
  a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
  pre {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    background: #07162c;
    color: #e3cf96;
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); }
</style>
